{
  "name": "VeeR EL2 TMR"
  "testpoints": [
    {
      "name": "baseline",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Prove that the design is capable of completing workloads from `software test suite` (STS)
        * Provide golden test results for comparison against tests with fault injection enabled

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Execute test software from STS on VeeR EL2
        * Do not inject any faults

        Check:
        * Verify the correctness of test software execution
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.1",
      "tests": [
        "test_baseline_workload_1",
        "test_baseline_workload_2",
        "test_baseline_workload_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["baseline"]
    },
    {
      "name": "fault_detection",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Prove that TMR logic is capable of detecting injected faults in the design
        * This should be treated as a smoke test for fault detection capabilities
        * Record `Time To Fault Event Detection`

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Generate multiple fault injection scenarios (FIS) with `faultergeist-gen` using one of available fault generation models
        * Use known seed values for generating fault injection strategies
        * Generate the minimal number of faults required to trigger Fault Event Detection
        * Enable fault injection for VeeR EL2 based on generated FIS
        * Execute test software from STS on VeeR EL2 for each generated FIS
        // Perhaps it would be sufficient to prepare only few places in the design
        // that are known to cause fault detection in TMR logic and use these for
        // fault injection.
        * Store `Time To Fault Event Detection` records as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and first Fault Event Detection
          * Record time between every successful Fault Event Recovery and subsequent Fault Event Detection

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic detects injected failures
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.2",
      "tests": [
        "test_fault_detection_workload_1",
        "test_fault_detection_workload_2",
        "test_fault_detection_workload_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["fault_detection"]
    },
    {
      "name": "recovery_success",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Prove that TMR logic is capable of recovering from detected Fault Event
        * Record `Time To Fault Event Detection`

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Generate multiple fault injection scenarios (FIS) with `faultergeist-gen` using one of available fault generation models
        * Use known seed values for generating fault injection strategies
        * Generate the minimal number of faults required to trigger Fault Event Detection
        * Enable fault injection for VeeR EL2 based on generated FIS
        * Execute test software from STS on VeeR EL2 for each generated FIS
        * Store `Time To Fault Event Detection` records as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and first Fault Event Detection
          * Record time between every successful Fault Event Recovery and subsequent Fault Event Detection

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic detects injected failures
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if TMR logic performs succesfull recovery from Fault Event
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Recovery Success Notification
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.3",
      "tests": [
        "test_recovery_success_workload_1",
        "test_recovery_success_workload_2",
        "test_recovery_success_workload_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["recovery_success"]
    },
    {
      "name": "recovery_success_directed",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Prove that TMR logic is capable of recovering from detected Fault Event
        * Prove the capabilities by testing on specified areas of the design
        * Record `Time To Fault Event Detection`

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Constrain the list of 'upsetable' signals only to considered design area
        * Generate multiple fault injection scenarios (FIS) with `faultergeist-gen` for each considered area and using one of available fault generation models
        * Use known seed values for generating fault injection strategies
        * Generate the minimal number of faults required to trigger Fault Event Detection
        * Enable fault injection for VeeR EL2 based on generated FIS
        * Execute test software from STS on VeeR EL2 for each generated FIS
        * Store `Time To Fault Event Detection` records as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and first Fault Event Detection
          * Record time between every successful Fault Event Recovery and subsequent Fault Event Detection

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic detects injected failures
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if TMR logic performs succesfull recovery from Fault Event
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Recovery Success Notification
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.3",
      "tests": [
        "test_recovery_success_directed_area_1_workload_1",
        "test_recovery_success_directed_area_2_workload_1",
        "test_recovery_success_directed_area_M_workload_1",
        "test_recovery_success_directed_area_1_workload_2",
        "test_recovery_success_directed_area_2_workload_2",
        "test_recovery_success_directed_area_M_workload_2",
        "test_recovery_success_directed_area_1_workload_N",
        "test_recovery_success_directed_area_2_workload_N",
        "test_recovery_success_directed_area_M_workload_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["recovery_success_directed"]
    },
    {
      "name": "recovery_failure",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Verify TMR logic behaviour upon detecting Fault Event that puts the design into unrecoverable state
        * Record `Time To Fault Event Detection`
        * Record `Time To Recovery Failure`

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Generate multiple fault injection scenarios (FIS) with `faultergeist-gen` using one of available fault generation models
        * Use known seed values for generating fault injection strategies
        * Generate the minimal number of faults required to trigger Fault Event Detection that leads to unrecoverable state
        * Enable fault injection for VeeR EL2 based on generated FIS
        * Execute test software from STS on VeeR EL2 for each generated FIS
        * Store `Time To Fault Event Detection` records as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and first Fault Event Detection
          * Record time between every successful Fault Event Recovery and subsequent Fault Event Detection
        * Store `Time To Recovery Failure` as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and Fault Event Detection that triggers Recovery Failure

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic detects injected failures
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if TMR logic detects unrecoverable failure
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Recovery Failed Notification
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.3",
      "tests": [
        "test_recovery_failure_workload_1",
        "test_recovery_failure_workload_2",
        "test_recovery_failure_workload_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["recovery_failure"]
    },
    {
      "name": "recovery_failure_directed",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Verify TMR logic behaviour upon detecting Fault Event that puts the design into unrecoverable state
        * Verify the capabilities by testing on specified areas of the design
        * Record `Time To Fault Event Detection`
        * Record `Time To Recovery Failure`

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Constrain the list of 'upsetable' signals only to considered design area
        * Generate multiple fault injection scenarios (FIS) with `faultergeist-gen` for each considered area and using one of available fault generation models
        * Use known seed values for generating fault injection strategies
        * Generate the minimal number of faults required to trigger Fault Event Detection that leads to unrecoverable state
        * Enable fault injection for VeeR EL2 based on generated FIS
        * Execute test software from STS on VeeR EL2 for each generated FIS
        * Store `Time To Fault Event Detection` records as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and first Fault Event Detection
          * Record time between every successful Fault Event Recovery and subsequent Fault Event Detection
        * Store `Time To Recovery Failure` as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and Fault Event Detection that triggers Recovery Failure

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic detects injected failures
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if TMR logic detects unrecoverable failure
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Recovery Failed Notification
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.3",
      "tests": [
        "test_recovery_failure_directed_area_1_workload_1",
        "test_recovery_failure_directed_area_2_workload_1",
        "test_recovery_failure_directed_area_M_workload_1",
        "test_recovery_failure_directed_area_1_workload_2",
        "test_recovery_failure_directed_area_2_workload_2",
        "test_recovery_failure_directed_area_M_workload_2",
        "test_recovery_failure_directed_area_1_workload_N",
        "test_recovery_failure_directed_area_2_workload_N",
        "test_recovery_failure_directed_area_M_workload_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["recovery_failure_directed"]
    },
    {
      "name": "critical_failure",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Verify design behaviour upon Fault Event that is not detected by TMR logic
        * Record `Time to Critical Failure`
        * Record fault vectors that triggered Critical Failure

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Generate multiple fault injection scenarios (FIS) with `faultergeist-gen` using one of available fault generation models
        * Use known seed values for generating fault injection strategies
        * Generate the minimal number of faults required to trigger Fault Event that is not detected by TMR logic and causes critical failure of the design
        * Enable fault injection for VeeR EL2 based on generated FIS
        * Execute test software from STS on VeeR EL2 for each generated FIS
        * Store `Time To Critical Failure` as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and Critical Failure
        * Store fault vectors that triggered Critical Failure as one of the test results

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic does not detect injected failures
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if design reached a critical failure
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.3",
      "tests": [
        "test_critical_failure_workload_1",
        "test_critical_failure_workload_2",
        "test_critical_failure_workload_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["critical_failure"]
    },
    {
      "name": "critical_failure_directed",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Verify design behaviour upon Fault Event that is not detected by TMR logic
        * Verify the behaviour on specified areas of the design
        * Record `Time to Critical Failure`

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Constrain the list of 'upsetable' signals only to considered design area
        * Generate multiple fault injection scenarios (FIS) with `faultergeist-gen` for each considered area and using one of available fault generation models
        * Use known seed values for generating fault injection strategies
        * Generate the minimal number of faults required to trigger Fault Event that is not detected by TMR logic and causes critical failure of the design
        * Enable fault injection for VeeR EL2 based on generated FIS
        * Execute test software from STS on VeeR EL2 for each generated FIS
        * Store `Time To Critical Failure` as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and Critical Failure
        * Store fault vectors that triggered Critical Failure as one of the test results

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic does not detect injected failures
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if design reached a critical failure
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.3",
      "tests": [
        "test_critical_failure_directed_area_1_workload_1",
        "test_critical_failure_directed_area_2_workload_1",
        "test_critical_failure_directed_area_M_workload_1",
        "test_critical_failure_directed_area_1_workload_2",
        "test_critical_failure_directed_area_2_workload_2",
        "test_critical_failure_directed_area_M_workload_2",
        "test_critical_failure_directed_area_1_workload_N",
        "test_critical_failure_directed_area_2_workload_N",
        "test_critical_failure_directed_area_M_workload_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["critical_failure_directed"]
    },
    {
      "name": "mtbf_measurement",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Gather from other tests:
          * `Time To Fault Event Detection`
          * `Time To Recovery Failure`
          * `Time To Critical Failure`
        * Aggregate results into Mean Time Between Failures grouped by:
          * Severity:
            * Fault Detection
            * Recovery Failure
            * Critical Failure
          * Area of fault injection
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.4",
      "tests": [
        "gather_mtbf_measurements"
      ]
      "tags": ["mtbf_measurement"]
    }
  ]
}
